# BMS Attendance — Backup / Recovery Note

## Working URLs
- QR generator: `https://rajendrieg.github.io/bms-attendance/qr-generator.html`
- Sign-in page: `https://rajendrieg.github.io/bms-attendance/signin.html`

## Current Working Flow
1. Lecturer opens `qr-generator.html`
2. Generates QR code for a session
3. Student scans QR and opens `signin.html`
4. Student enters student number and shares location
5. Sign-in redirects to Microsoft Form
6. Form response appears in Excel / AttendanceLog

## QR Generator Base URL
The QR generator must use:
`https://rajendrieg.github.io/bms-attendance/signin.html`

## Important Sign-in Page Requirements
- Must be valid HTML
- All CSS inside `<style>`
- All JS inside `<script>`
- QR parameters expected:
  - `s` = session ID
  - `subj` = subject
  - `type` = session type
  - `ven` = venue
  - `lat` = venue latitude
  - `lng` = venue longitude
  - `r` = venue radius
  - `t` = session start time
  - `w` = window minutes
- Minimum attendance window enforced: 90 minutes

## Microsoft Form / Logging
If AttendanceLog stops updating:
- Check Power Automate flow run history
- Confirm the form trigger is still active
- Confirm `Create item` to AttendanceLog still exists
- Confirm field mappings still match the list columns
- Check whether the lecturer email Outlook step changed the flow path

## SharePoint / AttendanceLog Columns
- Title
- StudentNumber
- SessionID
- Lat
- Lng
- AccuracyM
- DistanceM
- SignInStatus
- EntryMethod
- ManualReason
- ScanTimestamp
- Subject

## Quick Recovery Steps
If QR scanning fails:
1. Confirm scanned URL opens `signin.html`
2. Confirm GitHub Pages is serving the latest `signin.html`
3. Check browser console for JavaScript errors
4. Regenerate QR after refreshing `qr-generator.html`

If form logging fails:
1. Submit a test sign-in
2. Check Excel response capture
3. Check Power Automate flow run
4. Restore the SharePoint create-item step if needed
